! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F202A sub-tests 1-6, the
! START of the "COMPARE INDICATORS, AL, AE, AH" routine
! (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.30, octal 011301.00-011333.40).
! Companion to fp_compare_f202a.strap (A15-A20, extreme ranges): this
! block verifies the FP compare in the NORMAL exponent range and adds
! the AE (equal) outcome the extreme-range block did not reach.
!
! Six contiguous sub-tests, each load (unnormalized) / Z,$IND / compare
! (K, unnormalized) / three SIC-prefixed branch-on-indicator checks to
! the error routine SERS. The listing's own comment states the result:
!   A1: FPK0 vs FPK0  -> AE on (equal; both are zero)          BZAE,BAL,BAH
!   A2: FPK3 vs FPK0  -> AH on (FPK3 > 0)                       BZAH,BAL,BAE
!   A3: FPK0 vs FPK3  -> AL on (0 < FPK3)                       BZAL,BAE,BAH
!   A4: FPK3 vs FPK9  -> AH on (FPK3 > FPK9)                    BZAH,BAL,BAE
!   A5: FPK9 vs FPK3  -> AL on (FPK9 < FPK3)                    BZAL,BAE,BAH
!   A6: FPK3 vs FPK21 -> AL on ("memory opnd considered higher")BZAL,BAE,BAH
! A correct compare falls through all six to F202A7's location, where a
! PASS halt is substituted; a wrong indicator branches to SERS (a FAIL
! halt). PC alone says pass or fail.
!
! Substitutions (SSIP framework, at their real listed addresses so the
! SIC/branch machine code still matches the listing): SERS (octal 1304)
! -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch, PASS (octal 11334, where
! F202A7 begins) -> halt. Constants FPK0/FPK3/FPK9/FPK21 come from the
! pool on p.176 at octal 22005/22010/22016/22032.
!
! verify_fp_compare_a1_listing.py checks every transcribed half-word and
! constant bit-for-bit against the printed machine code.
!
! Observed: the model halts at PASS -- the FP compare sets exactly the
! expected indicator for the equal case (AE, via fpCompare returning 0
! on equal zero fractions) and for the normal-range greater/less cases.
! Injection (AE forced off in StretchExecute's FP compare arm, i.e.
! ind_AE never set): the model halts at SERS -- A1's BZAE branches to
! the error routine because AE is off, exactly as predicted. This
! discriminates the AE (equal) outcome specifically, which an AL/AH
! swap would not (equal is unaffected by swapping less/greater).
! Reversed by the exact inverse edit (AGENTS.md rule 2).

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool, p.176) --
        SLC, (8)22005.0
FPK0    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000000000000000000000
        SLC, (8)22010.0
FPK3    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000125252525252525240
        SLC, (8)22016.0
FPK9    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000125252525252525000
        SLC, (8)22032.0
FPK21   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031177777777777777767

! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)11301.0
F202A1  L(U), FPK0          ! AE ON  (equal)
        Z, $IND
        K(U), FPK0
        SIC, SEN
        BZAE, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAL, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAH, SERS
F202A2  L(U), FPK3          ! AH ON
        Z, $IND
        K(U), FPK0
        SIC, SEN
        BZAH, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAL, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAE, SERS
F202A3  L(U), FPK0          ! AL ON
        Z, $IND
        K(U), FPK3
        SIC, SEN
        BZAL, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAE, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAH, SERS
F202A4  L(U), FPK3          ! AH ON
        Z, $IND
        K(U), FPK9
        SIC, SEN
        BZAH, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAL, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAE, SERS
F202A5  L(U), FPK9          ! AL ON
        Z, $IND
        K(U), FPK3
        SIC, SEN
        BZAL, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAE, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAH, SERS
F202A6  L(U), FPK3          ! AL ON (memory opnd considered higher)
        Z, $IND
        K(U), FPK21
        SIC, SEN
        BZAL, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAE, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAH, SERS

! -- PASS halt where F202A7 begins --
        SLC, (8)11334.0
PASS    BEW, $

        END, F202A1
